## Brief Overview

---

Malaga Event Gear supplies an AV technician as part of specific event packages, never as a standalone hire, across Malaga and the wider Costa del Sol. Whether one is on site with your equipment depends on the package: included for the full event, included with an hour cap, available as a paid add on, or not offered at all.

This guide names exactly which package puts a technician on site, what that technician actually does while your event runs, and how far in advance to book one. [Contact us](/contact/) to confirm technician coverage for your date.

## Key Highlights

---

-   Four packages, four different technician outcomes: not offered, a paid add on, included for the full event, or included with an hour cap.

-   The [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) is the only package with a technician on site for the entire event, not a capped number of hours.

-   The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) includes a technician for up to 6 continuous hours, with each additional hour billed at 40 euros.

-   The [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) offers a technician as a paid add on, at 240 euros per day, rather than a standard inclusion.

-   We do not sell a technician on their own: every technician booking comes attached to one of our own equipment packages.

## Technician by Package: What's Included and What Costs Extra

Whether a technician is on site with your equipment is not a blanket rule. It is set per package, and the difference between "included" and "add on" is worth checking before you book, not after:

| Package | Technician | Cost | Coverage |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) | Not offered, not even as an add on | Not available | Not applicable |
| [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) | Paid add on | +240 euros per day | Full event day |
| [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) | Included | Included in the 650 euro package price | Full event, no hour cap |
| [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) | Included | Included in the 490 euro package price, +40 euros per extra hour | Up to 6 continuous hours |

All prices are ex VAT, with 21 percent Spanish VAT added at checkout. See full package inclusions on our [packages page](/packages/). If you also need the sound equipment specs behind each package, not just the technician column, our [sound system rental](/blog/sound-system-rental/) guide covers the same four packages by guest count and gear.

<InlineCTA />

## What an AV Technician Actually Does On Site

An AV technician is not just someone standing near the mixing desk. Before your event starts, they run gain staging and signal testing across the sound and any screens, catching a microphone that is about to feed back or a projector that will not sync before a single guest has arrived.

Once the event is live, they adjust gain as different speakers take the microphone, each with a different voice and a different distance from it, and manage the handoff as one speaker sits down and the next stands up, so a beat of silence never turns into dead air. If a wireless microphone connection drops, or a projector loses sync mid presentation, fixing it in the moment is their job, not something you troubleshoot from the audience.

That is the real difference between the packages that include a technician and the one that does not. On the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), the DJ or host runs their own set. On the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), one of our own crew is the one watching the levels for you.

## Can You Hire Just a Technician, Without the Equipment?

No. Malaga Event Gear does not sell a technician as a standalone service, only as part of one of our own equipment packages. If your event already has its own sound system, screen or lighting rig and you only need someone to operate it, that is not a booking we offer: our technicians are dispatched with our own gear, which is what they are trained on, not a third party rig they have never seen.

The closest match if a technician is your main requirement is the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/), where the technician is a paid add on rather than a standard inclusion, or the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) and [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), where one is already part of the package. [Contact us](/contact/) if you are unsure which package fits, and we will confirm what is and is not possible for your event.

## Wedding, Corporate or Party: Matching Technician Coverage to Your Event

Which package makes sense depends on how long your event actually needs a technician watching it, not just the type of event:

-   **A private party or DJ set** rarely needs a technician: the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) is a self run PA system, with the DJ or host controlling their own levels. See our [audio visual rental for music performances](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-music-performances/) guide.
-   **A wedding** runs ceremony, speeches, dinner and dancing back to back, often past the point a fixed hour cap would cover, which is why the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) includes a technician for the full event rather than a set number of hours.
-   **A board meeting or small client meeting** on the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) often does not need one on site at all, which is why it is an optional add on rather than a default inclusion.
-   **A larger conference, product launch or all hands meeting** on the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) gets a technician included for up to 6 continuous hours. If your event is likely to run longer, budget for the 40 euro per hour extension rather than assuming the cap will stretch.

For more on choosing between the Basic MICE Pack and the MICE Pack for a corporate event specifically, see our [audio visual rental for corporate meetings](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-corporate-meetings/) guide.

